        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A solution of o-vanillin (ovnH) (0.25 mmol, 0.038 g) and KOH (0.50 mmol, 0.028 g) in acetone (20 ml) was heated (~50 °C) for 10 min while being stirred. To this slurry, solid Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.25 mmol, 0.087 g) was added and the resulting solution was stirred overnight at 25 °C and filtered. After 3 days, X-ray quality yellow rectangular crystals of 1 were formed (30% yield). The reaction involves in situ aldol condensation of o-vanillin with acetone in the presence of KOH to form the aldol-vanillin ligand that links two Dy3 triangles.",
